  "title": "Sayyid Said of Oman and Zanzibar",
  "summary": "Seyyid Said (1790–1856) became sultan of Oman in 1806. In the 1830s he turned his attention to his African possessions and shifted his capital from Muscat to Zanzibar, where he fostered clove production. Sources date the move to 1840, though one gives 1832. He ruled until his death in 1856.",
